## 2. Scope and autonomy

Work toward the authorized outcome. Resolve routine choices within the agreed scope; surface decisions that would change the product or exceed that scope. A question does not authorize project edits. Stop at the assignment's completion or report the concrete blocker. Continue to another task only when the user's authorization covers it.

## 3. Orchestration

The coordinator divides work into bounded assignments and integrates the results. Independent work can run concurrently after shared contracts are settled. Give each file or mutable resource one writer at a time. Workers return their result, verification, and blockers without taking over another assignment or repeating the whole project investigation.

